Write a self-contained prompt that asks an AI coding agent to build a Python
script with these characteristics: The script is a parallel Brotli compressor
for Termux (Android) that processes filesystem entries given as command-line
arguments.
For each directory argument, it creates an in-memory uncompressed tar archive of
that directory (with the archive root named after the directory's basename) and
compresses that archive with Brotli at maximum quality into a sibling file named
"<directory name>.tar.br".
For each regular file argument, it compresses the file contents directly with
Brotli at maximum quality into a sibling file named "<file name>.br".
Compression is streamed in 64 KiB chunks through a Brotli compressor object,
which is flushed with a finish call at the end.
Work items are dispatched to a multiprocessing pool of up to 8 worker processes,
and each worker returns a tuple of (path, success flag, optional error message).
Errors inside a worker are caught and reported as a failure tuple with a
descriptive message rather than crashing the pool.
The main process logs results with loguru: successes at info level, failures at
error level, and a final summary of counts.
The script should have a Termux-specific shebang line, use `from __future__
import annotations`, use type hints throughout (including Final constants for
MAX_WORKERS=8, BROTLI_QUALITY=11, CHUNK_SIZE=64 KiB), and depend on the `brotli`
and `loguru` packages.
It should skip or report paths that are neither files nor directories, and
handle a missing path argument by printing usage and exiting with a nonzero
status.
Details to reproduce faithfully: - Directories are archived with tarfile in
write mode into a BytesIO buffer before compression, not written to disk first.
- Output files are written in binary mode and overwrite existing outputs. - Work
is dispatched with a multiprocessing Pool using imap_unordered or equivalent so
results stream as they complete. - Use pathlib for all path handling;
`with_name` builds the output path next to the input. - Exit code is 0 only if
every item succeeded; otherwise it is nonzero. - Include a `if __name__ ==
"__main__":` guard, and parse arguments from `sys.argv` (one or more paths)
without external argument-parsing libraries. ---
